    "body": "Thanks, this is definitely the right direction compared with removing `tree`.\r\nOne issue: the current compression only works when branch children are also leaves.\r\nFor a common shape like `root -> A -> [branch1 -> leaf1, branch2 -> leaf2]`,\r\n`leaf1` and `leaf2` disappear from the returned tree, while `activeLeafId`\r\nstill points at those leaf IDs. That means BranchNavigator can no longer build\r\nthe active path or navigate to the actual branch tail.\r\n\r\nI think the compressed tree needs to preserve a navigable target leaf per branch\r\n(or keep the leaf node itself), ideally with an iterative implementation so the\r\ncompression step itself cannot overflow on very long chains.",
